@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Sprint Planning & Backlog Management";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Sprint Planning and Backlog Management are key components of Agile project management. Azure Boards in Azure DevOps provides powerful tools to help teams plan sprints, organize work items, and track progress effectively.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Sprint Planning?</h2>
        <p>Sprint Planning is a meeting where the **Scrum Team** defines the work to be completed in the upcoming sprint. It ensures that the team has a clear understanding of what needs to be delivered.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Determines **which User Stories and Tasks** will be completed in the sprint.</li>
            <li>Ensures that the selected work aligns with the **team’s capacity and velocity**.</li>
            <li>Defines the **Sprint Goal**, providing a clear focus for the team.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/sprint-planning.png" alt="Sprint Planning in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Sprint Planning in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Steps in Sprint Planning</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Review the **Product Backlog** and identify high-priority items.</li>
                <li>Discuss each User Story to ensure clarity.</li>
                <li>Break down User Stories into **Tasks** for better tracking.</li>
                <li>Assign work items to team members.</li>
                <li>Set up the **Sprint Backlog** and define the **Sprint Goal**.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Backlog Management?</h2>
        <p>The Product Backlog is an **ordered list of work items** that need to be completed to improve a product. Effective backlog management ensures that development teams focus on the most important work.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Prioritizing work items based on **business value** and **customer needs**.</li>
            <li>Keeping backlog items **refined and well-documented**.</li>
            <li>Regularly reviewing and updating backlog priorities.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Managing the Backlog in Azure Boards</h4>
            <p>Azure Boards provides tools to streamline backlog management:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Use **Backlog Views** to organize work items efficiently.</li>
                <li>Leverage **Drag-and-Drop Prioritization** to reorder tasks quickly.</li>
                <li>Use **Epics and Features** to group related work items.</li>
                <li>Refine backlog items using **Sprint Refinement Meetings**.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/backlog-management.png" alt="Backlog Management in Azure Boards" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing the Product Backlog in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Tracking Sprint Progress</h2>
        <p>Once a sprint is planned, teams can use Azure Boards to track progress:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **Task Boards** to visualize work in progress.</li>
            <li>Monitor team performance using **Burndown Charts**.</li>
            <li>Use **Sprint Reviews and Retrospectives** to evaluate the sprint outcome.</li>
            <li>Adjust upcoming sprint planning based on past performance.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/burndown-chart.png" alt="Burndown Chart in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Tracking Sprint Progress with Burndown Charts</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Best Practices for Sprint Tracking</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Hold **daily stand-ups** to update progress and identify blockers.</li>
                <li>Regularly update work item statuses to maintain visibility.</li>
                <li>Use **cumulative flow diagrams** to track efficiency and bottlenecks.</li>
                <li>Ensure the **Sprint Backlog is realistic** and achievable.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Sprint Planning and Backlog Management are critical to Agile success. Azure Boards provides robust tools to help teams plan effectively, manage priorities, and track sprint progress seamlessly.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Boards, Queries, and Charts in Azure DevOps**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("WorkItemsEpicsFeaturesUserStories", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Work Items, Epics, Features, and User Stories</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("BoardsQueriesCharts", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Boards, Queries, and Charts &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>